msgid "Due-date notifications"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"KanbanMF can e-mail you about cards that are due soon or overdue. "
"Reminders are personal and per board: you decide for yourself, board by "
"board, whether you want them and when. Turning them on never subscribes "
"anyone else."
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting up your reminders for a board"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the board's menu — on its tile in the boards overview, or the ☰ at "
"the right of the board's bar — and choose :guilabel:`E-Mail "
"notification`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The My e-mail notifications dialog with reminders turned on."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reminders for one board."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Every change in this dialog is saved immediately; :guilabel:`Close` just "
"closes it."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`E-mail me about my due dates on this board`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Turns your reminders for this board on or off. The other settings appear "
"once it is on."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Notification hour`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The hour of the day the e-mails are sent, in your own time zone (see "
":doc:`preferences`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Send e-mails on`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The days of the week e-mails may be sent on — Monday to Friday by "
"default. A reminder that falls on any other day is skipped, not "
"postponed."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Notify these days before/after the due date`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Type a number and click **+** to add it. Negative numbers are days "
"*before* the due date, ``0`` is the day itself and positive numbers are "
"days after it. For example ``-3``, ``-1`` and ``0`` remind you three days"
" before, the day before, and on the day. Click the cross on a number to "
"remove it."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Send e-mails daily past … days the due date`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tick it and enter a number to keep getting a reminder every day once a "
"card is that many days overdue, until it is finished."
msgstr ""

msgid "Which cards you are reminded about"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only cards on that board that:"
msgstr ""

msgid "have you as an **assignee** — being a member is not enough;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"have a due date and **no end date** — once a card has an end date it is "
"finished and the reminders stop;"
msgstr ""

msgid "are not archived."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each e-mail is about one card. Its subject names the card and the board "
"and says how the card stands — due in a number of days, due today, or a "
"number of days late — and it links to the board. It is written in your "
"language."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You get at most one e-mail per card per day, even if several of your "
"rules match on the same day."
msgstr ""

msgid "When nothing arrives"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Check the e-mail days and the hour: reminders go out at the start of the "
"chosen hour, only on the chosen days."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check that you are an assignee of the card and that it has no end date."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reminders need the server to be able to send e-mail. If whoever runs your"
" KanbanMF hasn't set that up, no reminders are sent at all."
msgstr ""

